E-book fixtures for tests/ebook-calibre-sources.test.ts (docs/policy-decisions.md, entry 309)
================================================================================================

book-8bit.tcr (1,811 bytes), a Psion TCR book
  Written by calibre 8.5.0 (`ebook-convert book.txt book-8bit.tcr`) from the first 2,000 bytes of the plain text of
  `opf-lorem-ipsum-090.lit`, the Open Preservation Foundation format corpus (CC0 1.0, commit 366f068cec399d0cdfd61fa473de3ab6dc858098,
  ebooks/calibre 0.9.0/lorem-ipsum.lit; the text is "Variatio Ipsius" and lorem ipsum). No TCR book of a third party was found
  (bench/realworld/format-coverage-exceptions.json). calibre's TCR writer fails on the whole text of that book (4.4 KB) with
  `bytes must be in range(0, 256)`, so the book holds the first 2,000 bytes. The test decodes the container with a reader written from
  its layout (the signature `!!8-Bit!!`, a dictionary of 256 length-prefixed strings, the text as one dictionary index per byte).

hostile-links.chm (5,257 bytes), a Compiled HTML Help file whose first page links to a file of the host
  Hand-assembled uncompressed CHM (ITSF version 3, one PMGL listing chunk, content section 0 only) by generators/mkchm-links.py, the layout of
  tests/fixtures/archive-sources/generators/mkchm.py, with a #SYSTEM file (start page, table of contents), a two-entry table of contents
  and two pages. The first page names /etc/hosts as a picture, a style sheet and a link: by a relative path with twelve `..` segments, by a
  `file:///` URL and by an absolute path. Python 3.12: `python3 -I generators/mkchm-links.py` (run in this directory, with an `out/` directory).
  Read back with chmlib (python3-chm): and by calibre 8.5.0 and 7.6.0.

hostile-links.snb (492 bytes), a Bambook book whose one chapter links to files of the host
  Written by calibre's own SNBFile writer (the code of calibre 8.5.0 and of 9.x is the same there) through generators/mksnb-links.py, which loads
  `calibre/ebooks/snb/snbfile.py` by path and copies nothing of it. The chapter says "These are the visible words of the book." and names
  /etc/hosts and /etc/passwd as pictures: by an absolute path, by a relative path with twelve `..` segments and by a `file:///` URL. Read by calibre
  8.5.0 with the fix of scripts/calibre-patches (entry 465) to EPUB, text and OEB on the Linux testbed: the pictures stay dangling `src` attributes,
  no file of the host is read into the book (a PNG written beside the book was named the same three ways and was not embedded either).

